1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,360
The storm takes the power out at nine

2
00:00:02,360 --> 00:00:04,640
at night, and you're alone in a lift

3
00:00:04,640 --> 00:00:07,060
between the seventh floor and the eighth, with

4
00:00:07,060 --> 00:00:09,680
the powers of Killua from Hunter x Hunter.

5
00:00:10,460 --> 00:00:12,200
The emergency light flickers.

6
00:00:12,880 --> 00:00:13,720
The buttons are dead.

7
00:00:14,400 --> 00:00:16,440
You put your hand flat on the panel,

8
00:00:16,840 --> 00:00:19,740
and something in your arm goes cold, then

9
00:00:19,740 --> 00:00:20,000
bright.

10
00:00:20,640 --> 00:00:22,700
There's a crack, like a snapped twig.

11
00:00:23,420 --> 00:00:26,000
A blue line runs from your fingers into

12
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:26,440
the metal.

13
00:00:27,140 --> 00:00:28,080
The lights come back on.

14
00:00:28,080 --> 00:00:29,460
The lift starts moving.

15
00:00:30,260 --> 00:00:31,080
Nobody saw it.

16
00:00:31,540 --> 00:00:34,040
Your hair is standing straight up.

17
00:00:35,220 --> 00:00:37,520
In the story, Killua turns his own energy

18
00:00:37,520 --> 00:00:38,780
into electricity.

19
00:00:39,400 --> 00:00:40,740
Not a gadget, not a glove.

20
00:00:41,240 --> 00:00:42,160
Just his body.

21
00:00:42,880 --> 00:00:44,780
Over the next forty days you're going to

22
00:00:44,780 --> 00:00:47,300
learn what electricity can do inside a person,

23
00:00:47,300 --> 00:00:49,180
and what it takes back.

24
00:00:50,280 --> 00:00:53,180
In the story, that energy is called Nen,

25
00:00:53,520 --> 00:00:54,800
and it comes in six types.

26
00:00:55,240 --> 00:00:57,240
A simple test with a glass of water

27
00:00:57,240 --> 00:00:59,180
and a leaf shows which one is yours.

28
00:00:59,740 --> 00:01:01,640
You try it at your kitchen table, and

29
00:01:01,640 --> 00:01:03,780
the water changes in a way you can't

30
00:01:03,780 --> 00:01:04,340
explain.

31
00:01:04,920 --> 00:01:06,700
You're a Transmuter, like Killua.

32
00:01:07,220 --> 00:01:09,060
You don't make electricity out of nothing.

33
00:01:09,300 --> 00:01:11,760
You change what you already have into it.

34
00:01:12,320 --> 00:01:15,060
Rule one: the power isn't something you have.

35
00:01:15,440 --> 00:01:17,300
It's something your energy turns into.

36
00:01:18,460 --> 00:01:20,560
On day three you try to make a

37
00:01:20,560 --> 00:01:21,600
spark on purpose.

38
00:01:22,260 --> 00:01:24,240
It works, and it hurts.

39
00:01:24,900 --> 00:01:26,740
Your fingers sting for an hour.

40
00:01:27,680 --> 00:01:29,400
Killua doesn't feel it the way you do.

41
00:01:29,940 --> 00:01:31,420
In the story, he grew up in the

42
00:01:31,420 --> 00:01:33,500
Zoldyck family, a family of assassins,

43
00:01:34,220 --> 00:01:36,560
and his tolerance for electricity comes from a

44
00:01:36,560 --> 00:01:38,840
childhood of training you would never want.

45
00:01:39,440 --> 00:01:40,200
You don't have that.

46
00:01:40,660 --> 00:01:42,820
You have a stinging hand and a very

47
00:01:42,820 --> 00:01:43,720
confused cat.

48
00:01:44,560 --> 00:01:47,100
Rule two: the power hits the person who

49
00:01:47,100 --> 00:01:47,960
has it first.

50
00:01:48,920 --> 00:01:51,500
On day six you go to the aquarium,

51
00:01:51,500 --> 00:01:53,820
because you want to meet something that does

52
00:01:53,820 --> 00:01:54,760
this for a living.

53
00:01:55,760 --> 00:01:58,020
The electric eel in the tank doesn't look

54
00:01:58,020 --> 00:01:58,760
like much.

55
00:01:58,980 --> 00:02:02,600
But in 2019, scientists described a new species,

56
00:02:03,400 --> 00:02:06,160
Volta's electric eel, that can discharge up to

57
00:02:06,160 --> 00:02:08,060
eight hundred and sixty volts.

58
00:02:08,840 --> 00:02:10,375
That's more than the roughly six hundred and

59
00:02:10,375 --> 00:02:13,000
fifty of the eel everyone already knew about.

60
00:02:14,260 --> 00:02:16,360
A fish does that without training,

61
00:02:17,100 --> 00:02:20,120
without a family of assassins, without even trying.

62
00:02:20,820 --> 00:02:22,140
You stand there for a long time,

63
00:02:22,880 --> 00:02:24,720
a little jealous of a fish.

64
00:02:25,780 --> 00:02:26,300
Rule three:

65
00:02:27,140 --> 00:02:29,640
nature got there first, and it never brags

66
00:02:29,640 --> 00:02:30,460
about it.

67
00:02:31,240 --> 00:02:33,600
On day ten, in the park, a kid

68
00:02:33,600 --> 00:02:36,480
kicks a football way too hard, straight at

69
00:02:36,480 --> 00:02:36,840
a pram.

70
00:02:37,440 --> 00:02:38,080
You catch it.

71
00:02:38,940 --> 00:02:41,720
And the strange part is, you caught it

72
00:02:41,720 --> 00:02:43,080
before you decided to.

73
00:02:43,580 --> 00:02:45,720
A normal person needs about a quarter of

74
00:02:45,720 --> 00:02:47,380
a second to react to something they see.

75
00:02:48,140 --> 00:02:50,360
Studies put it somewhere between about a hundred

76
00:02:50,360 --> 00:02:52,160
and ninety and two hundred and eighty-five milliseconds.

77
00:02:53,000 --> 00:02:55,300
That's the delay between the eyes, the brain

78
00:02:55,620 --> 00:02:56,140
and the muscles.

79
00:02:56,900 --> 00:02:59,840
In the story, Killua's first Godspeed move, called

80
00:02:59,840 --> 00:03:03,100
Whirlwind, sends electrical signals straight to his muscles,

81
00:03:03,280 --> 00:03:05,160
so his body moves without waiting for that

82
00:03:05,160 --> 00:03:05,520
delay.

83
00:03:05,520 --> 00:03:08,740
Your hand just did the same thing.

84
00:03:09,440 --> 00:03:10,160
The mum thanks you.

85
00:03:10,600 --> 00:03:12,500
You don't tell her you're as shocked as

86
00:03:12,500 --> 00:03:13,300
she is.

87
00:03:14,000 --> 00:03:14,440
Rule four:

88
00:03:15,080 --> 00:03:17,400
the fastest thing in you isn't your legs.

89
00:03:18,100 --> 00:03:19,460
It's the delay you skip.

90
00:03:20,920 --> 00:03:23,460
The second half of Godspeed is called Speed

91
00:03:23,460 --> 00:03:26,040
of Lightning: it's about moving at that speed

92
00:03:26,040 --> 00:03:27,320
and staying in control.

93
00:03:28,060 --> 00:03:29,860
On day fifteen you try it on an

94
00:03:29,860 --> 00:03:30,660
empty running track.

95
00:03:31,360 --> 00:03:32,500
The start is incredible.

96
00:03:33,100 --> 00:03:35,080
The first bend is a disaster.

97
00:03:35,760 --> 00:03:38,420
You don't turn, you just keep going, straight

98
00:03:38,420 --> 00:03:39,040
into the fence.

99
00:03:39,940 --> 00:03:41,320
You lie on the grass looking at the

100
00:03:41,320 --> 00:03:43,880
sky, and you realise that being fast was

101
00:03:43,880 --> 00:03:44,600
the easy part.

102
00:03:45,800 --> 00:03:48,620
Rule five: speed you can't steer is just

103
00:03:48,620 --> 00:03:50,020
a crash with extra steps.

104
00:03:51,480 --> 00:03:54,740
On day twenty-two, a friend films your five-a-side

105
00:03:54,740 --> 00:03:55,060
game.

106
00:03:55,660 --> 00:03:56,160
You're in goal.

107
00:03:56,780 --> 00:03:59,300
Someone shoots from two metres away, and you

108
00:03:59,300 --> 00:03:59,800
save it.

109
00:04:00,580 --> 00:04:02,700
In slow motion, the ball hasn't even left

110
00:04:02,700 --> 00:04:04,540
their foot when your hand starts moving.

111
00:04:05,300 --> 00:04:06,420
The video goes everywhere.

112
00:04:06,880 --> 00:04:09,020
People argue that it's edited, people argue that

113
00:04:09,020 --> 00:04:11,540
it isn't, and a sports science lab sends

114
00:04:11,540 --> 00:04:13,060
you an email asking if you'd like to

115
00:04:13,060 --> 00:04:14,360
come in for a reaction test.

116
00:04:15,480 --> 00:04:15,880
You go.

117
00:04:16,580 --> 00:04:18,120
You try to be slow on purpose.

118
00:04:18,640 --> 00:04:20,220
You're slow on the first three tries, then

119
00:04:20,220 --> 00:04:22,420
your body forgets and catches the fourth one

120
00:04:22,420 --> 00:04:24,460
before the light even finishes turning green.

121
00:04:25,440 --> 00:04:26,960
The researcher doesn't say anything.

122
00:04:27,460 --> 00:04:29,480
She just writes for a very long time.

123
00:04:29,480 --> 00:04:32,840
Rule six: the world doesn't care how you

124
00:04:32,840 --> 00:04:33,380
do it.

125
00:04:33,660 --> 00:04:34,600
Only how often.

126
00:04:35,960 --> 00:04:38,600
On day twenty-six your best friend's little brother

127
00:04:38,600 --> 00:04:40,640
comes home with a torn jacket and a

128
00:04:40,640 --> 00:04:42,860
bruise, and everyone knows who did it.

129
00:04:43,280 --> 00:04:45,400
Your friend says it quietly, half joking:

130
00:04:46,160 --> 00:04:48,120
you could just give them a little shock.

131
00:04:48,820 --> 00:04:49,620
Nobody would ever know.

132
00:04:50,400 --> 00:04:51,000
And they're right.

133
00:04:51,600 --> 00:04:52,240
Nobody would know.

134
00:04:52,740 --> 00:04:53,880
That's what scares you.

135
00:04:54,500 --> 00:04:56,620
You think about Killua, a kid raised in

136
00:04:56,620 --> 00:04:57,700
a family of assassins.

137
00:04:57,700 --> 00:05:00,280
You realise that one shock like that would

138
00:05:00,280 --> 00:05:02,020
make you a little bit like them.

139
00:05:02,580 --> 00:05:02,960
You say no.

140
00:05:03,680 --> 00:05:04,560
Then you do the slow,

141
00:05:05,300 --> 00:05:05,300
boring,

142
00:05:05,940 --> 00:05:07,820
normal thing: you walk him to school every

143
00:05:07,820 --> 00:05:08,460
day that week.

144
00:05:09,160 --> 00:05:10,340
Nobody touches him again.

145
00:05:10,960 --> 00:05:13,300
Rule seven: a power is only as good

146
00:05:13,300 --> 00:05:15,080
as the things you refuse to do with

147
00:05:15,080 --> 00:05:15,360
it.

148
00:05:16,420 --> 00:05:19,700
In the story, Godspeed burns through Killua's electricity

149
00:05:19,700 --> 00:05:20,260
fast.

150
00:05:20,840 --> 00:05:23,180
Using it is easy; running out is the

151
00:05:23,180 --> 00:05:23,520
problem.

152
00:05:24,060 --> 00:05:25,940
You find that out on day thirty, when

153
00:05:25,940 --> 00:05:28,100
you use your power all day just because

154
00:05:28,100 --> 00:05:28,520
you can.

155
00:05:29,200 --> 00:05:30,620
By evening there's nothing left.

156
00:05:31,120 --> 00:05:32,880
No spark, no fast hand.

157
00:05:33,340 --> 00:05:35,060
You drop a cup and watch it break,

158
00:05:35,060 --> 00:05:36,720
at a normal person's speed.

159
00:05:37,200 --> 00:05:39,100
For the first time in a month, you're

160
00:05:39,100 --> 00:05:40,360
scared of being ordinary.

161
00:05:41,720 --> 00:05:44,520
On day forty there's a storm again, and

162
00:05:44,520 --> 00:05:46,320
it hits the funfair by the river.

163
00:05:46,940 --> 00:05:48,200
The power goes out.

164
00:05:48,640 --> 00:05:51,140
The ferris wheel stops, with people in every

165
00:05:51,140 --> 00:05:53,520
car, and the top ones are swinging in

166
00:05:53,520 --> 00:05:53,940
the wind.

167
00:05:54,700 --> 00:05:57,080
The engineers say it'll be an hour before

168
00:05:57,080 --> 00:05:57,980
the generator works.

169
00:05:58,720 --> 00:06:00,860
You put both hands on the control box,

170
00:06:01,360 --> 00:06:03,240
and you give it everything you've saved.

171
00:06:03,780 --> 00:06:04,520
The wheel moves.

172
00:06:05,340 --> 00:06:07,940
One car reaches the platform, and you let

173
00:06:07,940 --> 00:06:08,340
it go.

174
00:06:09,080 --> 00:06:09,620
Then the next.

175
00:06:10,160 --> 00:06:10,880
Then the next.

176
00:06:11,360 --> 00:06:13,780
By the last car your arms are shaking,

177
00:06:14,360 --> 00:06:16,180
the light in your hands is flickering like

178
00:06:16,180 --> 00:06:17,040
a dying bulb,

179
00:06:17,660 --> 00:06:19,900
and a little boy steps out holding his

180
00:06:19,900 --> 00:06:23,400
dad's hand and waves at the wheel, because

181
00:06:23,400 --> 00:06:25,540
he thinks the wheel did it.

182
00:06:25,680 --> 00:06:26,720
You let him think that.

183
00:06:27,700 --> 00:06:30,120
The next morning, a door slams in the

184
00:06:30,120 --> 00:06:32,340
corridor, and your hand is in the air

185
00:06:32,340 --> 00:06:33,780
before you've even heard it.

186
00:06:34,080 --> 00:06:35,820
That's the price nobody mentions.

187
00:06:36,420 --> 00:06:38,360
Your body reacts before you decide.

188
00:06:38,800 --> 00:06:42,040
Every noise, every movement, every time.

189
00:06:42,820 --> 00:06:44,080
You can't watch a scary film.

190
00:06:44,380 --> 00:06:45,440
You can't be surprised.

191
00:06:45,900 --> 00:06:47,580
You have to learn to be slow on

192
00:06:47,580 --> 00:06:50,420
purpose, all day, every day.

193
00:06:51,040 --> 00:06:53,500
Rule eight: the hardest part of being fast

194
00:06:53,500 --> 00:06:55,160
is choosing to wait.

195
00:06:56,420 --> 00:06:58,960
So if you woke up tomorrow with Killua's

196
00:06:58,960 --> 00:07:01,960
powers, would you take the speed or the

197
00:07:01,960 --> 00:07:02,220
spark?

198
00:07:02,980 --> 00:07:05,560
And what's the one thing you'd never use

199
00:07:05,560 --> 00:07:05,900
it for?

200
00:07:06,640 --> 00:07:07,440
Tell us in the comments.
